t its plan document must allow them. The same federal loan-limit formula applies to an owner-only plan, and a plan provision alone does not settle the prohibited-transaction requirements. Read the solo section of the 401(k) loan rules guide before using the calculator for a proposed loan."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What happens if I do not repay a 401(k) loan?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"A plan loan that fails to meet the qualifying loan rules can be treated as a distribution under 26 U.S.C. 72(p)(1). The calculator does not determine the tax consequences of a missed payment. Ask a tax professional to confirm those consequences, and use the 401(k) early withdrawal calculator for a tax estimate. Your plan document determines whether loans are offered, the interest rate, fees and any limit on the number of loans."}}]}</script><script type="application/ld+json">{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"BreadcrumbList","itemListElement":[{"@type":"ListItem","position":1,"name":"ModernWallet","item":"https://www.themodernwallet.com/"},{"@type":"ListItem","position":2,"name":"Retirement","item":"https://www.themodernwallet.com/retirement/"},{"@type":"ListItem","position":3,"name":"401k loan calculator","item":"https://www.themodernwallet.com/retirement/401k-loan-calculator/"}]}</script><script type="application/ld+json">{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"WebApplication","name":"401(k) Loan Calculator for Your Maximum Loan and Payment","description":"Use this 401(k) loan calculator to find your largest new loan and payment. Enter your vested balance, existing loans, past loan peak, rate and repayment term.","applicationCategory":"FinanceApplication","operatingSystem":"Any (web)","offers":{"@type":"Offer","price":0,"priceCurrency":"USD"},"url":"https://www.themodernwallet.com/retirement/401k-loan-calculator/"}</script><script type="application/ld+json">{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Person","name":"Jonathan Velez","url":"https://www.the